(go/type scoreAdjustTyp "These constants enumerate the set of possible ways/scenarios\nin which we'll adjust the score of a given callsite.\n" uint)























(go/const "These constants capture the various ways in which the inliner's\nscoring phase can adjust a callsite score based on heuristics. They\nfall broadly into three categories:\n\n1) adjustments based solely on the callsite context (ex: call\nappears on panic path)\n\n2) adjustments that take into account specific interesting values\npassed at a call site (ex: passing a constant that could result in\ncprop/deadcode in the caller)\n\n3) adjustments that take into account values returned from the call\nat a callsite (ex: call always returns the same inlinable function,\nand return value flows unmodified into an indirect call)\n\nFor categories 2 and 3 above, each adjustment can have either a\n\"must\" version and a \"may\" version (but not both). Here the idea is\nthat in the \"must\" version the value flow is unconditional: if the\ncallsite executes, then the condition we're interested in (ex:\nparam feeding call) is guaranteed to happen. For the \"may\" version,\nthere may be control flow that could cause the benefit to be\nbypassed.\n"

  ^{:line 48} [^{:tag scoreAdjustTyp :val 1 :doc "Category 1 adjustments (see above)\n"} panicPathAdj (<< 1 iota)]
  ^{:line 49} [^{:val 2} initFuncAdj]
  ^{:line 50} [^{:val 4} inLoopAdj]


  ^{:line 53} [^{:val 8 :doc "Category 2 adjustments (see above).\n"} passConstToIfAdj]
  ^{:line 54} [^{:val 16} passConstToNestedIfAdj]
  ^{:line 55} [^{:val 32} passConcreteToItfCallAdj]
  ^{:line 56} [^{:val 64} passConcreteToNestedItfCallAdj]
  ^{:line 57} [^{:val 128} passFuncToIndCallAdj]
  ^{:line 58} [^{:val 256} passFuncToNestedIndCallAdj]
  ^{:line 59} [^{:val 512} passInlinableFuncToIndCallAdj]
  ^{:line 60} [^{:val 1024} passInlinableFuncToNestedIndCallAdj]


  ^{:line 63} [^{:val 2048 :doc "Category 3 adjustments.\n"} returnFeedsConstToIfAdj]
  ^{:line 64} [^{:val 4096} returnFeedsFuncToIndCallAdj]
  ^{:line 65} [^{:val 8192} returnFeedsInlinableFuncToIndCallAdj]
  ^{:line 66} [^{:val 16384} returnFeedsConcreteToInterfaceCallAdj]

  ^{:line 68} [^{:val 32768} sentinelScoreAdj]) ; sentinel; not a real adjustment


;; This table records the specific values we use to adjust call
;; site scores in a given scenario.
;; NOTE: these numbers are chosen very arbitrarily; ideally
;; we will go through some sort of turning process to decide
;; what value for each one produces the best performance.

